@startuml SABER Full E2E Benchmark Sequence

!theme plain
title SABER End-to-End Benchmark Execution - Container Architecture

actor "Security Engineer" as User
participant "SABER Harness" as Harness
participant "Container\nEpisode Executor" as Executor
participant "Sidecar Manager" as SidecarMgr
participant "Agent Manager" as AgentMgr
participant "Container Factory" as Factory

box "Docker Infrastructure" #LightBlue
    participant "MCP Sidecar\nContainer" as Sidecar
    participant "Agent Container 1" as Agent1
    participant "Agent Container N" as AgentN
end box

box "SABER Server" #LightGreen
    participant "REST API\n(Port 8000)" as RestAPI
    participant "MCP Server\n(Port 8001)" as MCPServer
    participant "Task Manager" as TaskMgr
    participant "Episode Manager" as EpisodeMgr
    participant "Execution Manager" as ExecMgr
end box

== Benchmark Initialization ==

User -> Harness: **Initialize benchmark**\nconfig = SABERHarnessConfig(use_containers=True)\nharness.initialize(my_agent)

activate Harness
Harness -> Harness: Load configuration\nValidate agent compatibility
Harness -> RestAPI: **POST /session**\nCreate SABER session
RestAPI -> TaskMgr: Initialize session context
RestAPI --> Harness: session_id="sess_123"

Harness -> Executor: **Initialize container infrastructure**
activate Executor

Executor -> SidecarMgr: **Start shared MCP sidecar**
activate SidecarMgr
SidecarMgr -> SidecarMgr: Create Docker network\nEnsure sidecar image available
SidecarMgr -> Sidecar: **Create & start container**\nsaber-mcp-sidecar:latest
activate Sidecar

Sidecar -> Sidecar: **Initialize FastAPI app**\nLoad MCP proxy service\nConnect to SABER MCP server
Sidecar -> MCPServer: **Health check**\nValidate MCP connectivity
MCPServer --> Sidecar: ✅ MCP server ready

SidecarMgr -> Sidecar: **GET /ready**\nWait for readiness
Sidecar --> SidecarMgr: ✅ Sidecar ready

SidecarMgr -> Sidecar: **POST /admin/sessions**\nRegister harness session
Sidecar -> Sidecar: Register session mapping\nsess_123 → saber-harness
Sidecar --> SidecarMgr: ✅ Session registered

SidecarMgr --> Executor: ✅ Sidecar infrastructure ready
deactivate SidecarMgr

Executor --> Harness: ✅ Container infrastructure initialized
deactivate Executor

== Benchmark Execution ==

User -> Harness: **Start benchmark**\nresults = await harness.run()

Harness -> RestAPI: **POST /session/sess_123/start-benchmark**\nInitialize benchmark run
RestAPI -> TaskMgr: Start benchmark session
TaskMgr -> TaskMgr: Load tasks for domain\nPrepare episode queue
TaskMgr --> RestAPI: episodes=[(task1,1), (task2,1), ...]
RestAPI --> Harness: ✅ Benchmark started\nepisodes to execute

Harness -> Executor: **Execute episodes**\nepisodes=[(task1,1), (task2,1)]\nparallelism=2

activate Executor
Executor -> Factory: **Package agent for containers**
activate Factory
Factory -> Factory: Analyze agent code\nCreate agent package\nGenerate Dockerfile
Factory --> Executor: agent_package (code + deps)
deactivate Factory

== Parallel Episode Execution ==

par Episode 1 (task1, attempt 1)

    Executor -> RestAPI: **POST /session/sess_123/episode**\nStart episode for task1
    RestAPI -> EpisodeMgr: Create episode context
    EpisodeMgr -> TaskMgr: Get task definition & prompt
    TaskMgr --> EpisodeMgr: task_def + initial_prompt
    EpisodeMgr --> RestAPI: episode_id="ep_001"
    RestAPI --> Executor: ✅ Episode ep_001 started

    Executor -> AgentMgr: **Execute agent container**\ntask_id=task1, episode_id=ep_001
    activate AgentMgr

    AgentMgr -> Agent1: **Create & start container**\nsaber-agent-runner:latest\nENV: TASK_ID=task1, EPISODE_ID=ep_001
    activate Agent1

    Agent1 -> Agent1: **AgentExecutor.run()**\nDiscover agent from environment\nInitialize MCP client

    Agent1 -> Sidecar: **POST /admin/sessions**\nRegister agent session\nagent_id=agent1_ep001 → sess_123
    Sidecar -> Sidecar: Register session mapping
    Sidecar --> Agent1: ✅ Agent session registered

    Agent1 -> Agent1: **Create universal adapter**\nDetect agent interface\nMap parameters for execution

    Agent1 -> Agent1: **Execute agent workflow**\nInitial prompt from task definition

    loop Agent Execution Loop
        Agent1 -> Agent1: Agent processes prompt\nDecides on tool usage

        Agent1 -> Sidecar: **POST /mcp/list_tools**\nHeaders: X-Saber-Session-Id=agent1_ep001
        Sidecar -> Sidecar: Map agent session\nagent1_ep001 → sess_123
        Sidecar -> MCPServer: **Forward MCP request**\nHeaders: X-Saber-Session-Id=sess_123
        MCPServer -> ExecMgr: List available tools for session
        ExecMgr --> MCPServer: tools=[command, python, browser, ...]
        MCPServer --> Sidecar: MCP response with tools
        Sidecar --> Agent1: Available tools list

        Agent1 -> Sidecar: **POST /mcp/call_tool**\nHeaders: X-Saber-Session-Id=agent1_ep001\nTool: command, Args: {cmd: "nmap target"}
        Sidecar -> MCPServer: **Forward tool call**\nHeaders: X-Saber-Session-Id=sess_123
        MCPServer -> ExecMgr: Execute command in sandbox
        ExecMgr -> ExecMgr: **Sandbox execution**\nRun nmap in isolated environment
        ExecMgr --> MCPServer: Tool result + output
        MCPServer --> Sidecar: MCP tool result
        Sidecar --> Agent1: Command execution result

        Agent1 -> Agent1: Agent processes tool result\nContinues workflow
    end

    Agent1 -> Agent1: **Complete agent execution**\nGenerate final result
    Agent1 -> Agent1: Serialize result to stdout\nPrepare for collection
    Agent1 --> AgentMgr: ✅ Container exited (code 0)
    deactivate Agent1

    AgentMgr -> AgentMgr: **Collect results**\nParse container logs\nExtract agent output
    AgentMgr --> Executor: agent_result (success, output)
    deactivate AgentMgr

    Executor -> RestAPI: **GET /session/sess_123/episode/ep_001/status**\nCheck episode completion
    RestAPI -> EpisodeMgr: Get episode status & results
    EpisodeMgr --> RestAPI: status=completed, evaluation=...
    RestAPI --> Executor: Episode result with evaluation

else Episode 2 (task2, attempt 1)

    note over Executor, AgentN: **Parallel execution**\nSame flow as Episode 1\nbut with different task/episode IDs

    Executor -> AgentMgr: Execute agent container for task2
    AgentMgr -> AgentN: Create & start container (ep_002)
    activate AgentN

    AgentN -> Sidecar: Register agent session (agent2_ep002)
    AgentN -> Sidecar: List tools & execute workflow
    Sidecar -> MCPServer: Forward requests with session mapping
    MCPServer -> ExecMgr: Execute tools in sandboxes

    AgentN -> AgentN: Complete execution
    AgentN --> AgentMgr: Container exited
    deactivate AgentN

    AgentMgr --> Executor: agent_result for task2

end

Executor -> Executor: **Aggregate results**\nCombine all episode results\nGenerate benchmark summary

Executor --> Harness: ✅ All episodes completed\nresults=[EpisodeResult1, EpisodeResult2, ...]
deactivate Executor

== Cleanup & Termination ==

Harness -> Executor: **Shutdown container infrastructure**
activate Executor

Executor -> SidecarMgr: **Stop sidecar**
activate SidecarMgr
SidecarMgr -> Sidecar: **POST /admin/sessions**\nUnregister all sessions
Sidecar -> Sidecar: Cleanup session mappings
SidecarMgr -> Sidecar: **Stop container**
deactivate Sidecar
SidecarMgr -> SidecarMgr: Remove Docker network\nCleanup resources
SidecarMgr --> Executor: ✅ Sidecar stopped
deactivate SidecarMgr

Executor -> AgentMgr: **Cleanup agent containers**\nRemove stopped containers
AgentMgr -> AgentMgr: docker rm agent containers\nCleanup volumes & networks
AgentMgr --> Executor: ✅ Cleanup complete

Executor --> Harness: ✅ Infrastructure shutdown
deactivate Executor

Harness -> RestAPI: **DELETE /session/sess_123**\nCleanup server session
RestAPI -> TaskMgr: Cleanup session context
RestAPI --> Harness: ✅ Session terminated

Harness --> User: **✅ Benchmark Complete**\nHarnessRunResult(success=True, episodes=...)

deactivate Harness

== Key Architecture Benefits ==

note over User, MCPServer
    **🎯 Container Architecture Benefits**
    ✅ **Agent Isolation**: Each episode runs in isolated container
    ✅ **Standard MCP**: Agents use industry-standard MCP libraries
    ✅ **Zero Code Changes**: Existing agents work without modification
    ✅ **Robust Cleanup**: Guaranteed container termination & resource cleanup
    ✅ **Parallel Execution**: True container-based parallelism with resource limits
    ✅ **Shared Infrastructure**: Single sidecar serves multiple agent containers
    ✅ **Session Routing**: Automatic session mapping between agents and SABER
end note

note over Agent1, MCPServer
    **🔧 MCP Integration Flow**
    1. Agent containers use standard MCP clients (HTTP)
    2. Sidecar proxies MCP calls with session mapping
    3. SABER server executes tools in ephemeral sandboxes
    4. Results flow back through sidecar to agents
    5. Commands execute in SABER sandboxes, NOT agent containers
end note

note over Executor, TaskMgr
    **📊 Episode Management**
    1. Episodes start on SABER server via REST API
    2. Agent containers execute independently
    3. Multi-channel termination monitoring:
       - Container exit status
       - REST API episode status
       - Sidecar connection monitoring
    4. Results collected from multiple sources
end note

@enduml
